WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.929
ALEX VANCE: Out of the original Seven Wonders
cataloged by Greek travelers two

00:00:07.949 --> 00:00:11.110
ALEX VANCE: thousand years ago, earthquakes, fire,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.825
ALEX VANCE: and human greed destroyed six — leaving
only a 4,500-year-old limestone

00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:18.154
ALEX VANCE: mountain on the edge of Cairo.

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:21.677
DR. MAYA LIN: The question is simple: what did these
builders understand about stone,

00:00:21.697 --> 00:00:23.011
DR. MAYA LIN: weight, and time?

00:00:23.231 --> 00:00:27.219
ALEX VANCE: Hellenistic scholars chose the number
seven because in classical Greek

00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:30.597
ALEX VANCE: cosmology it represented completeness
and perfection:

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:33.575
ALEX VANCE: five known planets plus the Sun and
Moon.

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:40.557
DR. MAYA LIN: Built for Pharaoh Khufu under royal
vizier and chief architect Hemiunu,

00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:43.972
DR. MAYA LIN: the Great Pyramid stood 146.6 meters
tall —

00:00:43.992 --> 00:00:49.379
DR. MAYA LIN: remaining the tallest human-made
structure on Earth for more than 3,800 years.

00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:54.238
ALEX VANCE: Constructed over roughly twenty to
twenty-seven years during Egypt's Old

00:00:54.258 --> 00:00:58.195
ALEX VANCE: Kingdom around 2560 BCE, Khufu's horizon
monument,

00:00:58.215 --> 00:01:02.725
ALEX VANCE: originally named Akhet Khufu, crowned a
vast necropolis connected

00:01:02.745 --> 00:01:06.618
ALEX VANCE: directly to the Nile via artificial
harbor basins.

00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:09.304
DR. MAYA LIN: Across millennia of shifting empires,

00:01:09.324 --> 00:01:13.582
DR. MAYA LIN: earthquakes, and desert winds, the 7
Wonders of the World endure

00:01:13.602 --> 00:01:16.509
DR. MAYA LIN: as humanity's boldest signature in
stone.

00:01:16.529 --> 00:01:21.857
DR. MAYA LIN: Proof of what happens when geometry
and imagination refuse to accept the impossible.
